1
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:07,011
The team left us a mess.

2
00:00:07,011 --> 00:00:09,130
Where do we even begin?

3
00:00:09,667 --> 00:00:13,022
A team left you its repository in a bad state:

4
00:00:13,022 --> 00:00:17,035
meaningless commit messages, a password in the history,

5
00:00:17,035 --> 00:00:20,245
a large video in the history, no .gitignore,

6
00:00:20,245 --> 00:00:25,789
a version mismatch that fails CI, a feature branch that conflicts with main,

7
00:00:25,789 --> 00:00:28,415
a badly named tag, and no CI at all.

8
00:00:28,415 --> 00:00:34,251
Turn it into a professional GitHub repository with a complete delivery pipeline:

9
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:37,904
Assess the damage.

10
00:00:39,667 --> 00:00:46,136
The password is fake here; with a real one, rotate it first (lesson 89).

11
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:48,796
At the stop:

12
00:00:48,796 --> 00:00:55,220
undo the image tag change, keep the latte price, and give the commit a proper message:

13
00:00:56,967 --> 00:01:00,246
Ignore what never belongs in the repository.

14
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:09,831
The chai branch also changed the latte price (3.50 vs 3.30 on main).

15
00:01:09,831 --> 00:01:12,594
The team agreed on 3.40:

16
00:01:14,333 --> 00:01:19,682
Everything local is fixed except what only exists after the pull requests:

17
00:01:19,682 --> 00:01:23,441
chai and the workflows on main, and the release tag.

18
00:01:23,441 --> 00:01:25,393
Part 2 does that on GitHub.

19
00:01:27,133 --> 00:01:30,183
Create the repository and push main.

20
00:01:31,933 --> 00:01:34,822
Pull requests required (0 approvals:

21
00:01:34,822 --> 00:01:39,796
a solo learner cannot approve their own PRs; a team uses 1–2),

22
00:01:39,796 --> 00:01:47,498
the checks job required and up to date, rules enforced for admins, no force pushes or deletions:

23
00:01:49,233 --> 00:01:55,418
The checks run on the pull request; wait for them, add a review comment, merge:

24
00:01:57,167 --> 00:02:05,531
(The last line comes from gh updating your local main after the squash merge.) A direct push to main is now impossible,

25
00:02:05,531 --> 00:02:06,866
even for the owner:

26
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:11,180
The tag starts the release workflow:

27
00:02:11,180 --> 00:02:16,841
checks, image build and push to GHCR, a GitHub release with the packaged chart,

28
00:02:16,841 --> 00:02:24,724
then a deploy job that creates a kind cluster on the runner, pulls the image from GHCR and installs the chart:

29
00:02:26,467 --> 00:02:28,176
Final check.
